# Modules

If it has lifecycle, retained state, or input, it is a **class with a closed boundary**. `Session` constructs it and subscribes (`onLookAt`, `onSelectMap`, …). Session never grabs a child canvas or implements that widget's pointer machine.

```
app/      Pixi boot + ticker. No feature code.
session/  Running match: map load, input routing, subscriptions.
sim/      Deterministic world. No Pixi, fetch, or DOM.
render/   Pixi drawing. Reads views, does not mutate sim.
ui/       DOM widgets (Hud, Minimap). Own their DOM and input.
```

Classes for `Session`, `World`/`MapGrid`, `Clock`, `Renderer`, `Camera`, `Hud`, `Minimap`, `MapInput`. Functions for pure math (`gridToWorld`, `treeSheetAt`, dump parse).

```ts
// BAD — session reaches into the widget
hud.minimap.addEventListener("pointerdown", ...)
paintMinimap(hud.minimap, view)

// GOOD
new Minimap(host, { onLookAt: (x, y) => session.lookAt(x, y) })
minimap.setView(view)
```
